# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
#
# Everything here is produced from the sources and weighs far more than them. The three
# MazeForge .pdb files alone are 195 MB; a repository that carries them gets slow in a week
# and never gets fast again.
#
# A bare directory name matches at any depth, so this covers both the project's own folders
# and the ones inside Plugins/MazeForge.

Binaries/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Build/

# Logs, autosaves, crash reports, the cooked output. None of it is a source, and Saved/ is
# also where the editor writes while it runs — tracking it means a dirty tree at all times.
Saved/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated project files
#
# UnrealBuildTool regenerates these from the .uproject and the .Build.cs files. Right-click
# the .uproject and choose "Generate Visual Studio project files" after a fresh clone.

*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editors and IDEs

.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- operating systems

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- not ignored, on purpose
#
# Content/ IS tracked, including Content/MazeForge/Maps and Content/MazeForge/Meshes, which
# the export regenerates. They are ~400 KB today and a checkout that includes them is a
# checkout that opens without errors — MainLevel names those sublevels, and without them the
# map complains on load.
#
# The trade is binary churn: every Apply Changes rewrites a dozen .uasset and .umap files,
# and git stores each version whole. If the repository ever gets heavy, the fix is to add
#
#     Content/MazeForge/Maps/
#     Content/MazeForge/Meshes/
#
# here and accept that a fresh clone needs one Apply Changes before MainLevel is happy.

Claude outputs/
